// Models live in per-domain files alongside this one (tenant, staff, customer, admin, fleet, trip, notification, analytics).
//
// Tenancy rules every tenant-owned model follows:
// 1. It has a tenantId, even child tables like TripStop. Tenant filtering (and RLS, if we add it) never needs a join.
// 2. It exposes @@unique([tenantId, id]), and relations between tenant-owned models reference (tenantId, id) instead
//    of id alone. The database then rejects any row pointing across tenants, whatever the application code does.
// 3. Optional relations use onDelete: Restrict. Prisma's default for them, SetNull, would also try to null tenantId.
// 4. Uniqueness is per tenant (@@unique([tenantId, ...])), unless a value has to be global (staff emails, storage keys).
//
// Platform-level models (Tenant itself, Admin*, AuditLog) have no tenantId.

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client"
  output   = "../../generated/prisma"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
}
